# Retrieval

## Overview

The retrieval index holds chunk embeddings for every ingested document. A query re-ranks the top candidates against the question before returning them.

## Key technical decisions

### Chunk size is fixed at ingestion

The index holds 42,000 chunks today, each capped at 512 tokens. A larger chunk raises recall and blurs the boundary a citation should point at, so ingestion splits every document at a fixed size rather than one derived from its own structure.
